				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$z\left(\vartheta \right)=\left\{\begin{array}{cc}{\omega }_{z} &amp; {\rm{if}}\,0\le \vartheta &lt; {\vartheta }_{{G}_{1}/S}\\ 0 &amp; {\rm{if}}\,{\vartheta }_{{G}_{1}/S}\le \vartheta &lt; 2\pi \end{array},\right.$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M64"><mml:mi>z</mml:mi><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mfenced open="{"><mml:mrow><mml:mtable><mml:mtr><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ω</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>z</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mtd><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">if</mml:mi><mml:mspace width="0.25em"/><mml:mn>0</mml:mn><mml:mo>≤</mml:mo><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi><mml:mo>&lt;</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>G</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:mi>S</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mtd></mml:mtr><mml:mtr><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:mtd><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">if</mml:mi><mml:mspace width="0.25em"/><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>G</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:mi>S</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>≤</mml:mo><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi><mml:mo>&lt;</mml:mo><mml:mn>2</mml:mn><mml:mi>π</mml:mi></mml:mtd></mml:mtr></mml:mtable><mml:mo>,</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced></mml:math><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="anchor" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ6.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ6.gif?><?image-size 2568?><?image-md5 c4450fcc43aaf286195e6df095e59338?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 51?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c4450fcc43aa/41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ6.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ6.gif?><?thumb-size 2568?><?thumb-md5 c4450fcc43aaf286195e6df095e59338?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 51?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c4450fcc43aa/41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ6.gif?></graphic></alternatives></disp-formula>where <inline-formula id="IEq27"><alternatives><tex-math id="M65"><?equation-image-name M65.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 636653e0a5bb2bbbb8d05a1052ad0f48?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/636653e0a5bb/M65.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\omega }_{z}\in {{\mathbb{R}}}_{+}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M66"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ω</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>z</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>∈</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>+</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq27.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq27.gif?><?image-size 330?><?image-md5 a81092e41d8c8feebaddbbde3faf4476?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 59?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/a81092e41d8c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq27.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq27.gif?><?thumb-size 330?><?thumb-md5 a81092e41d8c8feebaddbbde3faf4476?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 59?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/a81092e41d8c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq27.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is the angular velocity added to the cell cycle phase dynamics when the cell is fed with methionine-free medium.</p><p id="Par42">Our agent-based model also considers cell division events. Indeed, when a cell passes through the M to G<sub>1</sub> transition (<inline-formula id="IEq28"><alternatives><tex-math id="M67"><?equation-image-name M67.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 40985c14182e986d2b76a3e45720a8bd?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/40985c14182e/M67.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\vartheta }_{M/{G}_{1}}=2\pi$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M68"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>M</mml:mi><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>G</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>2</mml:mn><mml:mi>π</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq28.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq28.gif?><?image-size 2738?><?image-md5 2e6c13547b511765ce3ed4b64c2e6fc2?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 70?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/2e6c13547b51/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq28.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq28.gif?><?thumb-size 2738?><?thumb-md5 2e6c13547b511765ce3ed4b64c2e6fc2?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 70?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/2e6c13547b51/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq28.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>) then a new cell (i.e. a new agent) is added to the model. The initial condition of the daughter cell depends on the state of the mother cell. Specifically, the initial phase is set to <inline-formula id="IEq29"><alternatives><tex-math id="M69"><?equation-image-name M69.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 c786530974c07da08b59f0fe6bdfaec0?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c786530974c0/M69.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\vartheta }_{0}=0$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M70"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq29.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq29.gif?><?image-size 300?><?image-md5 4649d470c7516076f8fa0b0deb6a63da?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 50?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/4649d470c751/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq29.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq29.gif?><?thumb-size 300?><?thumb-md5 4649d470c7516076f8fa0b0deb6a63da?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 50?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/4649d470c751/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq29.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>, while the initial volume is set to <inline-formula id="IEq30"><alternatives><tex-math id="M71"><?equation-image-name M71.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 9938c3e1cf770f997dbe2436305d98c3?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/9938c3e1cf77/M71.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${V}_{0}= 0.61 {V}_{M/{{G}_{1}}}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M72"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>V</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>0.61</mml:mn><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>V</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>M</mml:mi><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>G</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq30.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq30.gif?><?image-size 571?><?image-md5 61058a51adc145c798bda8783d177f7c?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 30?><?image-scaled-width 112?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/61058a51adc1/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq30.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq30.gif?><?thumb-size 571?><?thumb-md5 61058a51adc145c798bda8783d177f7c?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 30?><?thumb-scaled-width 112?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/61058a51adc1/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq30.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>, where <inline-formula id="IEq31"><alternatives><tex-math id="M73"><?equation-image-name M73.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 5aa9dcacffea7b67d71dbcbb54e0b514?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/5aa9dcacffea/M73.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${V}_{M{/}{G}_{1}}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M74"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>V</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>M</mml:mi><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>G</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq31.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq31.gif?><?image-size 298?><?image-md5 79d593ecb35ccbdaf991eb4168e9b453?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 45?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/79d593ecb35c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq31.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq31.gif?><?thumb-size 298?><?thumb-md5 79d593ecb35ccbdaf991eb4168e9b453?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 45?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/79d593ecb35c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq31.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is the volume of the mother cell at the division time (i.e. at the M/G<sub>1</sub> transition). Therefore, the number of cells in our agent-based model is an increasing value.</p><p id="Par43">The parameter values used in the agent model of the non-cycling strain are <inline-formula id="IEq32"><alternatives><tex-math id="M75"><?equation-image-name M75.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 0db440d9e7a5205d09630bf4cf91dcaa?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/0db440d9e7a5/M75.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${V}_{c}=1$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M76"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>V</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>c</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq32.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq32.gif?><?image-size 245?><?image-md5 11dd697d1dbbe0f69e072efae563f468?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 49?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/11dd697d1dbb/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq32.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq32.gif?><?thumb-size 245?><?thumb-md5 11dd697d1dbbe0f69e072efae563f468?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 49?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/11dd697d1dbb/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq32.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (critical volume), <inline-formula id="IEq33"><alternatives><tex-math id="M77"><?equation-image-name M77.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 f345095dd98a4d51e0f4bff90a06823f?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f345095dd98a/M77.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\beta =0.0083{\rm{mi}}{{\rm{n}}}^{-1}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M78"><mml:mi>β</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>0.0083</mml:mn><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">mi</mml:mi><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">n</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>−</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msup></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq33.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq33.gif?><?image-size 716?><?image-md5 047905b097dab87a4c0214bfe1047c5e?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 35?><?image-scaled-width 121?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/047905b097da/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq33.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq33.gif?><?thumb-size 716?><?thumb-md5 047905b097dab87a4c0214bfe1047c5e?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 35?><?thumb-scaled-width 121?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/047905b097da/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq33.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (volume growth rate; see ref. <sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR31">31</xref></sup>), <inline-formula id="IEq34"><alternatives><tex-math id="M79"><?equation-image-name M79.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 74d094d0ce9b45f6d79d0d026290e8ee?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/74d094d0ce9b/M79.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$T=75\,{\rm{min}}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M80"><mml:mi>T</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>75</mml:mn><mml:mspace width="0.25em"/><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">min</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq34.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq34.gif?><?image-size 2363?><?image-md5 f4a41ca19a9e02bb7f5f5248aa45c60c?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 72?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f4a41ca19a9e/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq34.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq34.gif?><?thumb-size 2363?><?thumb-md5 f4a41ca19a9e02bb7f5f5248aa45c60c?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 72?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f4a41ca19a9e/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq34.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (nominal cell cycle period; see ref. <sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR36">36</xref></sup>), <inline-formula id="IEq35"><alternatives><tex-math id="M81"><?equation-image-name M81.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 6cfc1283820d0fc3107e6baf16d12e0c?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/6cfc1283820d/M81.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\omega }_{z}=\frac{2\pi }{T}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M82"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ω</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>z</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mfrac><mml:mrow><mml:mn>2</mml:mn><mml:mi>π</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>T</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:mfrac></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq35.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq35.gif?><?image-size 313?><?image-md5 464f7dc96c1a74be70f0ce512be16bcb?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 36?><?image-scaled-width 56?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/464f7dc96c1a/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq35.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq35.gif?><?thumb-size 313?><?thumb-md5 464f7dc96c1a74be70f0ce512be16bcb?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 36?><?thumb-scaled-width 56?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/464f7dc96c1a/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq35.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (angular velocity in methionine-free medium), and <inline-formula id="IEq36"><alternatives><tex-math id="M83"><?equation-image-name M83.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 88d8663ec8ae2b2ce1d18acb79404875?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/88d8663ec8ae/M83.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\vartheta }_{{G}_{1}/S}=\frac{\pi }{2}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M84"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>G</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:mi>S</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mfrac><mml:mrow><mml:mi>π</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>2</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:mfrac></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq36.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq36.gif?><?image-size 2424?><?image-md5 2ac599cb1ddda5d733a4c0a722476561?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 80?><?image-scaled-width 189?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/2ac599cb1ddd/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq36.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq36.gif?><?thumb-size 2424?><?thumb-md5 2ac599cb1ddda5d733a4c0a722476561?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 189?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/2ac599cb1ddd/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq36.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (phase value at G<sub>1</sub>/S transition; see ref. <sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR45">45</xref></sup>). The parameter values used in the agent model of the cycling strain are: <inline-formula id="IEq37"><alternatives><tex-math id="M85"><?equation-image-name M85.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 0db440d9e7a5205d09630bf4cf91dcaa?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/0db440d9e7a5/M85.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
