				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$t$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M210"><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq92.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq92.gif?><?image-size 127?><?image-md5 a9ec1de4f07d4138723851503cd41823?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 9?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/a9ec1de4f07d/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq92.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq92.gif?><?thumb-size 127?><?thumb-md5 a9ec1de4f07d4138723851503cd41823?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 9?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/a9ec1de4f07d/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq92.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>.</p></sec><sec id="Sec14"><title>Quantification of synchronisation</title><p id="Par47">To quantify the degree of cell cycle synchronisation across the cell population, we computed two synchronisation indices: a) the mean coherence phase <inline-formula id="IEq93"><alternatives><tex-math id="M211"><?equation-image-name M211.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 dc3eae884ab8d5b20ab952b6ba821ccd?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/dc3eae884ab8/M211.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$R$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M212"><mml:mi>R</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq93.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq93.gif?><?image-size 158?><?image-md5 41ee29614678fe697b91f1fa512f92da?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 15?><?image-scaled-width 15?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/41ee29614678/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq93.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq93.gif?><?thumb-size 158?><?thumb-md5 41ee29614678fe697b91f1fa512f92da?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 15?><?thumb-scaled-width 15?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/41ee29614678/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq93.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> of the Kuramoto order parameter<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR47">47</xref></sup> and b) the amplitude Power of the leading peak in the power spectrum of the average YFP fluorescence signal.</p><p id="Par48">The mean phase coherence <inline-formula id="IEq94"><alternatives><tex-math id="M213"><?equation-image-name M213.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 deda99e101b8d26020d579ab66db3095?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/deda99e101b8/M213.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
