				\begin{document}$$\psi \in [{\mathrm{0,2}}\pi]$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M216"><mml:mi>ψ</mml:mi><mml:mo>∈</mml:mo><mml:mrow><mml:mo>[</mml:mo><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">0, 2</mml:mi><mml:mi>π</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mo>]</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq95.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq95.gif?><?image-size 2926?><?image-md5 a2e00a545f33e70e98e580ce6a99c1bf?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 74?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/a2e00a545f33/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq95.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq95.gif?><?thumb-size 2926?><?thumb-md5 a2e00a545f33e70e98e580ce6a99c1bf?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 74?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/a2e00a545f33/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq95.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> are defined as the magnitude and argument of the Kuramoto order parameter, respectively<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR47">47</xref></sup>:<disp-formula id="Equ14"><label>14</label><alternatives><tex-math id="M217"><?equation-image-name M217.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 f0f5567afea7d632fab2285765342f0f?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f0f5567afea7/M217.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
