				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$R$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M230"><mml:mi>R</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq101.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq101.gif?><?image-size 158?><?image-md5 41ee29614678fe697b91f1fa512f92da?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 15?><?image-scaled-width 15?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/41ee29614678/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq101.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq101.gif?><?thumb-size 158?><?thumb-md5 41ee29614678fe697b91f1fa512f92da?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 15?><?thumb-scaled-width 15?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/41ee29614678/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq101.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is equal to 0, cells are totally desynchronised.</p><p id="Par49">The amplitude <inline-formula id="IEq102"><alternatives><tex-math id="M231"><?equation-image-name M231.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 6743a2f377bac0c0ec71c59d0afa8703?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/6743a2f377ba/M231.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\rm{Power}}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M232"><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">Power</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq102.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq102.gif?><?image-size 333?><?image-md5 882d6e1f2cb2406b5223dfe3197b406a?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 48?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/882d6e1f2cb2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq102.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq102.gif?><?thumb-size 333?><?thumb-md5 882d6e1f2cb2406b5223dfe3197b406a?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 48?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/882d6e1f2cb2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq102.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> of the leading peak is computed from the power spectral density (PSD) of the normalised YFP fluorescence signal. Specifically, the mean of the average YFP signal is subtracted from the signal itself, then the MATLAB function <italic toggle="yes">pmcov</italic> of the <italic toggle="yes">Signal Processing Toolbox</italic> is used to compute the parametric estimation of the PSD. The leading peak of the PSD is found with the MATLAB function <italic toggle="yes">max</italic>. The leading peak in the PSD is associated to a specific period. We decided to discard a peak value associated to a period longer than the duration of the YFP signal. In this case, we classified that peak as not determined (N.D.).</p></sec><sec id="Sec15"><title>Control algorithms</title><p id="Par50">All control algorithms were devised to change the control input (i.e., the growth medium) once a new system output (i.e., the estimated cell cycle phases) was available. Moreover, the control input was held constant between two consecutive phase measurement times (zero-order hold method<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR48">48</xref></sup>). All control algorithms were implemented through custom scripts in the MATLAB environment. The illustrative code for each control algorithm is available at <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://github.com/dibbelab/Cycloop/tree/main/Illustrative_Platform_Code">https://github.com/dibbelab/Cycloop/tree/main/Illustrative_Platform_Code</ext-link>.</p><sec id="Sec16"><title>Stop&amp;go control</title><p id="Par51">The stop&amp;go control algorithm is an event-triggered feedback control strategy that was devised to synchronising the cell cycle across a population of non-cycling cells<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR42">42</xref></sup>. At each sampling time <inline-formula id="IEq103"><alternatives><tex-math id="M233"><?equation-image-name M233.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 3cde260dd5540b39262b2a6e61c0e76c?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/3cde260dd554/M233.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${t}_{k}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M234"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq103.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq103.gif?><?image-size 161?><?image-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 15?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq103.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq103.gif?><?thumb-size 161?><?thumb-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 15?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq103.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>, the stop&amp;go algorithm computes the percentage of cells in the G<sub>1</sub> phase by means of the estimated cell cycle phases (see Phase estimation and budding index section). If the percentage of cells in the G<sub>1</sub> phase is higher than a fixed threshold <inline-formula id="IEq104"><alternatives><tex-math id="M235"><?equation-image-name M235.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 aa32b4de23b81ee1fd40750918fcedaa?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/aa32b4de23b8/M235.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\nu }_{ \% }$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M236"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ν</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>%</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq104.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq104.gif?><?image-size 187?><?image-md5 f53d015f62d2352c11e01844e91db0f8?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 22?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f53d015f62d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq104.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq104.gif?><?thumb-size 187?><?thumb-md5 f53d015f62d2352c11e01844e91db0f8?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 22?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f53d015f62d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq104.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>, then the algorithm delivers a −MET pulse of duration <inline-formula id="IEq105"><alternatives><tex-math id="M237"><?equation-image-name M237.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 bdfc932836d7e35b05810863ed7e6a03?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/bdfc932836d7/M237.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${D}_{-{Met}}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M238"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>D</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>−</mml:mo><mml:mi>M</mml:mi><mml:mi>e</mml:mi><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq105.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq105.gif?><?image-size 289?><?image-md5 ab106eef7491652d4f1bc4459532f172?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 45?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/ab106eef7491/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq105.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq105.gif?><?thumb-size 289?><?thumb-md5 ab106eef7491652d4f1bc4459532f172?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 45?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/ab106eef7491/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq105.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> to the cells, otherwise cells are kept in +MET medium. Controller’s parameters used in our implementation were: <inline-formula id="IEq106"><alternatives><tex-math id="M239"><?equation-image-name M239.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 021d9f9da7b9c458c457cf79ab63bfbc?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/021d9f9da7b9/M239.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\nu }_{ \% }=50 \%$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M240"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ν</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>%</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>50</mml:mn><mml:mi>%</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq106.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq106.gif?><?image-size 2139?><?image-md5 b35f94ca5bbda2248b6648131421b92b?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 80?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/b35f94ca5bbd/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq106.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq106.gif?><?thumb-size 2139?><?thumb-md5 b35f94ca5bbda2248b6648131421b92b?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/b35f94ca5bbd/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq106.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (threshold value) and <inline-formula id="IEq107"><alternatives><tex-math id="M241"><?equation-image-name M241.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 0cdb71a483d89d7a50479745515cbedf?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/0cdb71a483d8/M241.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${D}_{-{{\rm{Met}}}}=30\,{{\min }}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M242"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>D</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>−</mml:mo><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">Met</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>30</mml:mn><mml:mspace width="0.25em"/><mml:mi>min</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq107.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq107.gif?><?image-size 545?><?image-md5 ab3f977b0d04aedf6935a657113243ac?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 30?><?image-scaled-width 112?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/ab3f977b0d04/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq107.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq107.gif?><?thumb-size 545?><?thumb-md5 ab3f977b0d04aedf6935a657113243ac?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 30?><?thumb-scaled-width 112?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/ab3f977b0d04/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq107.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>(duration of −MET pulse). Note that <inline-formula id="IEq108"><alternatives><tex-math id="M243"><?equation-image-name M243.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 0480aaa87bc35f9fc3c702c1ddbaa324?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/0480aaa87bc3/M243.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\nu }_{ \% }=100 \%$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M244"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ν</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>%</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>100</mml:mn><mml:mi>%</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq108.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq108.gif?><?image-size 2881?><?image-md5 670bbbdb65648c83f05f49aebeaa8ded?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 70?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/670bbbdb6564/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq108.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq108.gif?><?thumb-size 2881?><?thumb-md5 670bbbdb65648c83f05f49aebeaa8ded?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 70?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/670bbbdb6564/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq108.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> in the ideal implementation illustrated in Fig. <xref rid="Fig3" ref-type="fig">3a</xref>.</p></sec><sec id="Sec17"><title>Reference oscillator</title><p id="Par52">The reference oscillator strategy is a state feedback control strategy that was devised to synchronise the cell cycle across a population of cells. We adapted the control strategy proposed by Bai and Wen<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR38">38</xref></sup> to design a state feedback control law able to steer the cell cycle phases to converge towards a reference phase. Here, the reference phase evolves over time according to the dynamics of a virtual phase oscillator that interacts with all the cells in the population through a virtual star-like coupling. We constructed the virtual reference oscillator through an ODE model that describes the evolution of the reference oscillator phase <inline-formula id="IEq109"><alternatives><tex-math id="M245"><?equation-image-name M245.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 4b73768a714e01a4321ac2ec63ae05d5?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/4b73768a714e/M245.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\vartheta }_{r}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M246"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq109.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq109.gif?><?image-size 187?><?image-md5 c3faa317168c9b4e09cd0a6f37e9997e?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 20?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c3faa317168c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq109.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq109.gif?><?thumb-size 187?><?thumb-md5 c3faa317168c9b4e09cd0a6f37e9997e?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 20?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c3faa317168c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq109.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> on the unit circle <inline-formula id="IEq110"><alternatives><tex-math id="M247"><?equation-image-name M247.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 0f6d459d22f65de29aa7cddf59eb13ef?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/0f6d459d22f6/M247.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${{\mathbb{S}}}^{1}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M248"><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">S</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msup></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq110.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq110.gif?><?image-size 192?><?image-md5 2f613a39bd509422102a21a747c2337b?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 35?><?image-scaled-width 20?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/2f613a39bd50/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq110.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq110.gif?><?thumb-size 192?><?thumb-md5 2f613a39bd509422102a21a747c2337b?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 35?><?thumb-scaled-width 20?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/2f613a39bd50/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq110.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> over time:<disp-formula id="Equ15"><label>15</label><alternatives><tex-math id="M249"><?equation-image-name M249.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 6c9a67b120ad9a548cb1e74add7dd3c6?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/6c9a67b120ad/M249.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\frac{{\rm{d}}}{{{\rm{d}}t}}\vartheta_{r}={\omega }_{r}+\gamma \mathop{\sum }\limits_{m=1}^{N}{{\sin }}\left({\vartheta }_{m}-{\vartheta }_{r}\right),$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M250"><mml:mfrac><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">d</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">d</mml:mi><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:mfrac><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ω</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>+</mml:mo><mml:mi>γ</mml:mi><mml:munderover accent="false" accentunder="false"><mml:mrow><mml:mo>∑</mml:mo></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:munderover><mml:mi>sin</mml:mi><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>−</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mo>,</mml:mo></mml:math><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="anchor" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ15.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ15.gif?><?image-size 2248?><?image-md5 d37eededc52425aba8e27e43ccde8460?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 60?><?image-scaled-width 200?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/d37eededc524/41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ15.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ15.gif?><?thumb-size 2248?><?thumb-md5 d37eededc52425aba8e27e43ccde8460?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 60?><?thumb-scaled-width 200?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/d37eededc524/41467_2021_22689_Article_Equ15.gif?></graphic></alternatives></disp-formula>where <inline-formula id="IEq111"><alternatives><tex-math id="M251"><?equation-image-name M251.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 90b675c04a4c0d8c094edaf9d6711d75?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/90b675c04a4c/M251.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\omega }_{r}\in {{\mathbb{R}}}_{+}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M252"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ω</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>∈</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>+</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq111.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq111.gif?><?image-size 2189?><?image-md5 7edf750669d8a433912259d7d0703da4?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 80?><?image-scaled-width 165?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/7edf750669d8/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq111.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq111.gif?><?thumb-size 2189?><?thumb-md5 7edf750669d8a433912259d7d0703da4?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 165?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/7edf750669d8/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq111.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is the natural frequency of the reference oscillator, <inline-formula id="IEq112"><alternatives><tex-math id="M253"><?equation-image-name M253.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 4c2f12112a248c87d847f031b36987d1?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/4c2f12112a24/M253.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\gamma \in {{\mathbb{R}}}_{+}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M254"><mml:mi>γ</mml:mi><mml:mo>∈</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>+</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq112.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq112.gif?><?image-size 341?><?image-md5 7e06af2c3119b8c19ca6c70fba4e1bd4?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 52?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/7e06af2c3119/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq112.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq112.gif?><?thumb-size 341?><?thumb-md5 7e06af2c3119b8c19ca6c70fba4e1bd4?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 52?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/7e06af2c3119/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq112.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is the coupling strength, <inline-formula id="IEq113"><alternatives><tex-math id="M255"><?equation-image-name M255.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 f5cc413938a5dad7c78e3be2c4470c5b?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f5cc413938a5/M255.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$N{\mathbb{\in }}{\mathbb{N}}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M256"><mml:mi>N</mml:mi><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">\in</mml:mi><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">N</mml:mi></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq113.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq113.gif?><?image-size 298?><?image-md5 c6c5aeef20ec289deb82ee9e194033b2?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 39?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c6c5aeef20ec/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq113.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq113.gif?><?thumb-size 298?><?thumb-md5 c6c5aeef20ec289deb82ee9e194033b2?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 39?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/c6c5aeef20ec/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq113.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is the number of cells and <inline-formula id="IEq114"><alternatives><tex-math id="M257"><?equation-image-name M257.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 e4ac69c9f10574889fc3e3000ca47ed2?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/e4ac69c9f105/M257.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\vartheta }_{m}\in {{\mathbb{S}}}^{1}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M258"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>∈</mml:mo><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="double-struck">S</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msup></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq114.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq114.gif?><?image-size 360?><?image-md5 74da9e1752f49f08c09da51968cfe547?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 35?><?image-scaled-width 58?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/74da9e1752f4/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq114.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq114.gif?><?thumb-size 360?><?thumb-md5 74da9e1752f49f08c09da51968cfe547?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 35?><?thumb-scaled-width 58?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/74da9e1752f4/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq114.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> is the cell cycle phase of the <italic toggle="yes">m</italic>th cell in the population. Note that the number of cells changes over time at each sampling time <inline-formula id="IEq115"><alternatives><tex-math id="M259"><?equation-image-name M259.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 3cde260dd5540b39262b2a6e61c0e76c?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/3cde260dd554/M259.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${t}_{k}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M260"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq115.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq115.gif?><?image-size 161?><?image-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 15?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq115.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq115.gif?><?thumb-size 161?><?thumb-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 15?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq115.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> (see Phase estimation and budding index section). Moreover, the cell cycle phases were held constant between two consecutive phase measurement times (zero-order hold method<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="CR48">48</xref></sup>). At each sampling time <inline-formula id="IEq116"><alternatives><tex-math id="M261"><?equation-image-name M261.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 3cde260dd5540b39262b2a6e61c0e76c?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/3cde260dd554/M261.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${t}_{k}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M262"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq116.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq116.gif?><?image-size 161?><?image-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 15?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq116.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq116.gif?><?thumb-size 161?><?thumb-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 15?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq116.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>, the algorithm first measures the cell cycle phases through the phase estimation algorithm (see Phase estimation and budding index section). Let <inline-formula id="IEq117"><alternatives><tex-math id="M263"><?equation-image-name M263.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 e268b352f1bb30ff4d42b94de25147d5?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/e268b352f1bb/M263.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${N}_{k}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M264"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq117.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq117.gif?><?image-size 213?><?image-md5 f3f91f6ffa0692a5ff59c83b2c3810d3?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 22?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f3f91f6ffa06/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq117.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq117.gif?><?thumb-size 213?><?thumb-md5 f3f91f6ffa0692a5ff59c83b2c3810d3?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 22?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/f3f91f6ffa06/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq117.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> be the number of cells whose phases have been measured at the sampling time <inline-formula id="IEq118"><alternatives><tex-math id="M265"><?equation-image-name M265.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 3cde260dd5540b39262b2a6e61c0e76c?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/3cde260dd554/M265.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${t}_{k}$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M266"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq118.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq118.gif?><?image-size 161?><?image-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 15?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq118.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq118.gif?><?thumb-size 161?><?thumb-md5 91183ac754d2377bddd16525ae28bc27?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 15?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/91183ac754d2/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq118.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula>. Then, the algorithm computes the control action <inline-formula id="IEq119"><alternatives><tex-math id="M267"><?equation-image-name M267.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 250e46e7916862fbe3d4ed9bc26be567?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/250e46e79168/M267.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$u\left({t}_{k}\right)$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M268"><mml:mi>u</mml:mi><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq119.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq119.gif?><?image-size 301?><?image-md5 6216254703adddd0795529918bafc444?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 38?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/6216254703ad/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq119.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq119.gif?><?thumb-size 301?><?thumb-md5 6216254703adddd0795529918bafc444?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 38?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/6216254703ad/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq119.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> to apply to the cell population in the interval <inline-formula id="IEq120"><alternatives><tex-math id="M269"><?equation-image-name M269.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 3d199a847ef32769e6fc59af8e3881af?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/3d199a847ef3/M269.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$[{t}_{k},{t}_{k+1}]$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M270"><mml:mrow><mml:mo>[</mml:mo><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mo>,</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi><mml:mo>+</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow><mml:mo>]</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:math><inline-graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq120.gif"><?image-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq120.gif?><?image-size 334?><?image-md5 8405a53a868c03b8ac082455b5eb8558?><?image-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?image-scaled-height 29?><?image-scaled-width 58?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/8405a53a868c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq120.gif?><?thumb-name 41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq120.gif?><?thumb-size 334?><?thumb-md5 8405a53a868c03b8ac082455b5eb8558?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 29?><?thumb-scaled-width 58?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/8405a53a868c/41467_2021_22689_Article_IEq120.gif?></inline-graphic></alternatives></inline-formula> through the state feedback control law:<disp-formula id="Equ16"><label>16</label><alternatives><tex-math id="M271"><?equation-image-name M271.gif?><?equation-image-status READY?><?equation-image-md5 47199d413dce2df64289954335a82be5?><?equation-image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/4187/8079375/47199d413dce/M271.gif?>\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$u\left({t}_{k}\right)=\left\{\begin{array}{cc}{u}_{{{\rm{OFF}}}}{=}^{{\prime} }+{{\rm{MET}}}^{{\prime} }, &amp; {\rm{if}}\mathop{\sum }\limits_{m=1}^{{N}_{k}}{a}_{m}\left({t}_{k}\right){{\sin }}\left({\vartheta }_{m}\left({t}_{k}\right)-{\vartheta }_{r}\left({t}_{k}\right)\right)\ge 0\\ {u}_{{{\rm{ON}}}}{=}^{{\prime} }-{{\rm{MET}}}^{{\prime} }, &amp; {\rm{if}}\mathop{\sum }\limits_{m=1}^{{N}_{k}}{a}_{m}\left({t}_{k}\right){{\sin }}\left({\vartheta }_{m}\left({t}_{k}\right)-{\vartheta }_{r}\left({t}_{k}\right)\right) &lt; 0\end{array}\right.,$$\end{document}</tex-math><mml:math xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="M272"><mml:mi>u</mml:mi><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mfenced open="{"><mml:mrow><mml:mtable><mml:mtr><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>u</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">OFF</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mo>=</mml:mo></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>′</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msup><mml:mo>+</mml:mo><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">MET</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>′</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msup><mml:mo>,</mml:mo></mml:mtd><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">if</mml:mi><mml:munderover accent="false" accentunder="false"><mml:mrow><mml:mo>∑</mml:mo></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:munderover><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>a</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mi>sin</mml:mi><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mo>−</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mo>≥</mml:mo><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:mtd></mml:mtr><mml:mtr><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>u</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">ON</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mo>=</mml:mo></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>′</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msup><mml:mo>−</mml:mo><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">MET</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>′</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:msup><mml:mo>,</mml:mo></mml:mtd><mml:mtd columnalign="center"><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">if</mml:mi><mml:munderover accent="false" accentunder="false"><mml:mrow><mml:mo>∑</mml:mo></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:munderover><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>a</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:mfenced><mml:mi>sin</mml:mi><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ϑ</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>m</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:msub><mml:mfenced close=")" open="("><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mi>t</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mi>k